From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: register slave mii bus through OF on 5.4

On 5.4 __mdiobus_register() has no of_node branch, so calling
mdiobus_register() for the slave MDIO bus never instantiates the PHYs
described under the switch's "mdio" child node.  PHYs such as the
AN7583 internal GPHYs carry an explicit "ethernet-phy-idXXXX.YYYY"
compatible (they boot powered down and cannot be probed by reading
registers 2/3), so they would never get a driver.

Use of_mdiobus_register() when the "mdio" child exists.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
--- a/net/dsa/dsa2.c	2026-10-09 15:20:26.335262740 +0800
+++ b/net/dsa/dsa2.c	2026-10-09 15:20:26.335262740 +0800
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <linux/rtnetlink.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_net.h>
+#include <linux/of_mdio.h>
 #include <net/devlink.h>
 
 #include "dsa_priv.h"
@@ -367,6 +368,7 @@
 
 static int dsa_switch_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
 {
+	struct device_node *mdio_np;
 	int err = 0;
 
 	/* Initialize ds->phys_mii_mask before registering the slave MDIO bus
@@ -404,7 +406,17 @@
 
 		dsa_slave_mii_bus_init(ds);
 
-		err = mdiobus_register(ds->slave_mii_bus);
+		/* Register through the OF-aware path when the switch node has
+		 * an "mdio" child: on 5.4 mdiobus_register() alone never
+		 * instantiates the DT-described PHYs (__mdiobus_register has
+		 * no of_node branch here), so PHYs carrying an explicit
+		 * "ethernet-phy-idXXXX.YYYY" compatible would never appear.
+		 */
+		mdio_np = of_get_child_by_name(ds->dev->of_node, "mdio");
+		if (mdio_np)
+			err = of_mdiobus_register(ds->slave_mii_bus, mdio_np);
+		else
+			err = mdiobus_register(ds->slave_mii_bus);
 		if (err < 0)
 			goto teardown;
 	}
